<title>RUSSIA: Fourth Russian sugar test has 13.1 pct content.</title>
<headline>Fourth Russian sugar test has 13.1 pct content.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's fourth sugar beet test showed a sugar content of 13.1 percent, the same as in 1995, Alexander Nechosov, the deputy head of the Semsvyokla sugar beet seed producers' association, said on Monday.</p>
<p>He gave the following data for the test, which was conducted by August 20 -</p>
<p>				   4th 1996 test	 4th 1995 test</p>
<p> Avg sugar content	   13.1 pct		13.1 pct</p>
<p> Beet weight (grams)	 284		     318</p>
<p> Beets per hectare	   65,000		  68,000</p>
<p>&quot;The results of the fourth test confirm the worrying forecast for the whole year... The beet is just too dry due to the lack of moisture in the ground,&quot; Nechosov said.</p>
<p>This is the fourth test to measure sugar content, but the sixth test overall.</p>
<p>Farmers sowed sugar beet to 1.03 million hectares this year, slightly below a targeted level of 1.11 million ha.</p>
<p>--Dmitry Solovyov, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
